  Text:
    m_Untranslated: '<b>1</b>.  Watch the video above.


      <b>2</b>.  In the <b>Project</b> window, open the <b>Assets</b> > <b>Prefabs</b> folder.


      <b>Important</b>: Single-click, don''t double-click, the stairs asset (<a href="https://learn.unity.com/tutorial/671be8afedbc2a0105a17c0e#671bf065edbc2a0105919b3b">Help</a>).


      <b>3</b>.  In the <b>Project</b> window, select the <b>Stairs</b> GameObject and drag it onto the ground in the <b>Scene</b> view.


      <b>Note</b>: Don''t worry that the stairs are on their side; you''ll fix that later!

'
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-4572812623835632559
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "You now know the fundamentals of working in 3D, well done! \n\nYou might not feel confident yet, but that's OK. It'll take time and practice to really feel comfortable using the skills you just learned. \n\nTo continue your learning journey, begin the next tutorial: \"Explore the possibilities.\""
--- !u!114 &-4307483210042323010
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: INSTRUCTIONS
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>1</b>.  In either the <b>Hierarchy</b> window or the <b>Scene</b> view, select the <b>Stairs</b> GameObject. \n\n<b>2</b>.  Select the <b>Rotate</b> tool from the <b>Tool</b> overlay.\n\n<b>3</b>.  Select and drag the handles of the <b>Rotate</b> gizmo to rotate the stairs so they\u2019re the right way up and at the correct angle.\n\n<b>Tip</b>: Click and drag in a straight line instead of trying to rotate around the GameObject.\n\n<b>4</b>.  Enter Play mode and have the robot collect the third star.\n\n<b>5</b>.  Remember to save your scene as you make changes.\n"
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
--- !u!114 &-4236620108765180388
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "You're now familiar with the basic parts of the Unity Editor.\n\nIn this tutorial, you'll learn to navigate in 3D space and manipulate GameObjects in a scene. \n\nLet's get started."
--- !u!114 &-3930552556311075639
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: INSTRUCTIONS
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>1</b>.  Select the <b>Cube</b> GameObject you just added.\n\n<b>2</b>.  Select the <b>Scale</b> tool from the <b>Tool</b> overlay.\n\n<b>3</b>.  Select and drag the handles of the <b>Scale</b> gizmo to change the dimensions of the cube. \n\n<b>4</b>.  Use the <b>Move</b>, <b>Rotate</b>, and <b>Scale</b> tools to change the cube into a ramp to the other platform.\n\n<b>Important</b>: Transforming a cube can be very frustrating, especially when you\u2019re just getting the hang of the <b>Move</b>, <b>Rotate</b>, and <b>Scale</b> tools, but it\u2019s worth testing out your skills.\n\n<b>5</b>.  Enter Play mode and have the robot collect the last star.\n\n<b>6</b>.  When you\u2019re finished, don\u2019t forget to exit Play mode."
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
